---
import Arrow from './Arrow.astro';
import catalog from '../content/packs.json';
import { loadPacks } from '../lib/packs';
const packs = loadPacks(catalog);
const guide = 'https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/blob/shrek/docs/puzzle-authoring.md';
---
<section id="puzzle-packs" class:list={['packs-section', 'wrap', { 'packs-with-downloads': packs.length > 0 }]} aria-labelledby="packs-title">
  <div class="pack-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Share a little paper</span>
    <h2 id="packs-title">Make a puzzle pack.</h2>
    <p>Have a pattern in mind? Turn it into a paper someone else can solve. Start with our example pack, try your own folds, and send it for review.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href={guide}>A guide to making packs <Arrow /></a>
    <details class="pack-details">
      <summary>How to submit a pack <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
      <div class="pack-detail-body">
        <ol>
          <li>Fork <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude">Orifude on GitHub</a> and copy the <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/tree/shrek/puzzles/example-pack">example pack</a> into <code>community/your-pack-id/1.0.0/</code>.</li>
          <li>Edit the puzzles and <code>pack.toml</code>. Include your name and a license that allows redistribution. Play every puzzle, then run <code>orifude verify PATH</code> and <code>orifude solve PATH</code> on the folder.</li>
          <li>Open a <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/compare/shrek...shrek?expand=1&amp;template=puzzle-pack.md">pack pull request</a> from your fork to <code>shrek</code>. Include the command results, play notes, and source credits.</li>
          <li>Isolated CI runs the validator and solver. A maintainer reviews the puzzles, text, and license before publishing a versioned ZIP and checksum here.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </details>
    <p class="small-copy pack-offline">You can also keep your creations to yourself. Every pack plays offline.</p>
  </div>
  {packs.length > 0 && <div class="pack-downloads" aria-label="Reviewed puzzle packs">
    {packs.map((pack) => <article class="pack-download">
      <span class="eyebrow">Reviewed puzzle pack · {pack.version}</span>
      <h3>{pack.title}</h3>
      <p class="pack-description">{pack.description}</p>
      <p class="small-copy pack-credit">{pack.puzzles} puzzles by {pack.authors.join(', ')}<br />{pack.license} · Orifude 1.0.0 or later</p>
      <div class="pack-actions">
        <a class="button" href={pack.zipUrl}>Download {pack.title} ZIP <Arrow direction="down" /></a>
        <a class="small-copy" href={pack.checksumUrl}>SHA-256 checksums</a>
      </div>
      <details class="pack-details">
        <summary>How to install <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="pack-detail-body">
          <p>Download the ZIP and checksum file, then <a href={`${guide}#download-and-install-a-published-pack`}>check the SHA-256 checksum</a>. Install the ZIP with:</p>
          <pre><code>orifude pack install FILENAME.zip</code></pre>
          <p>Open Orifude and choose Puzzle packs. To update a pack, remove the installed version first. Your saved progress and keepsakes remain.</p>
          <p class="pack-links"><a href={pack.releaseUrl}>Release and review</a><a href={pack.sourceUrl}>Pack source</a></p>
          <p class="pack-hash small-copy">ZIP SHA-256<br /><code>{pack.sha256}</code></p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </article>)}
  </div>}
</section>
